<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 12:39:54 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Spain's Sanchez says no 'solid proof' that Morocco planned Ceuta crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis</link><description>
Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez has told lawmakers that there is no evidence the Ceuta migrant crisis was orchestrated by Morocco's government. His remarks come a day after tens of thousands of people took part in protests across the country to criticize his handling of the migrant influx. He acknowledged that Ceuta was both a humanitarian crisis and an administrative challenge. But he rejected the findings of a police report that seemed to lay blame on Morocco. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5bde64-8ce1-11f1-a75a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T112414Z-409645030-RC2ZOMA4UF9K-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5bde64-8ce1-11f1-a75a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T112414Z-409645030-RC2ZOMA4UF9K-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a2d278a-a785-11f1-b12a-3bc92fe369a2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 11:58:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Meloni government sets longevity record in Italy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy</link><description>
Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government has been in power for 1,413 days. She surpassed the record set by Silvio Berlusconi between 2001 and 2005, making her government Italy's longest serving uninterrupted government since World War II, after a period of intense instability. Italy has had 68 governments in the last 80 years. Giorgia Meloni and her party will celebrate the feat on Friday with a huge pre-election rally in the southern city of Bari. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta tells more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e304d96-8ce6-11f1-8b95-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B87T4P8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e304d96-8ce6-11f1-8b95-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B87T4P8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba705724-a778-11f1-8437-61d24622b9c9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:11:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Norway seizes Russian ship to enforce $4.22 billion Ukrainian compensation claim</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim</link><description>
Norway said Wednesday it had seized a Russian ship as part of a Ukrainian effort to recover $4.22 billion awarded to state energy firm Naftogaz over Russia’s seizure of its assets in Crimea in 2014. The Professor Molchanov vessel was detained off the Arctic Svalbard archipelago after a Norwegian court ordered its arrest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1ee5b0e-a779-11f1-a62b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246257525164.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1ee5b0e-a779-11f1-a62b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246257525164.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c3a36fe-a77a-11f1-b953-6be120fbcf4d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:07:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1ee5b0e-a779-11f1-a62b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246257525164.jpg">© Mindaugas Kulbis, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>No 'solid proof' Morocco planned Ceuta migrant rush, says Spanish PM Sanchez</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description>
Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said Thursday there was no "solid proof" that Morocco orchestrated a migrant rush into Ceuta in July following the emergence of a police report highlighting multiple failings by Moroccan security forces.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff8ec802-a76b-11f1-9b93-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T071929Z-2098391657-RC2JBNAFLHWL-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff8ec802-a76b-11f1-9b93-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T071929Z-2098391657-RC2JBNAFLHWL-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22c65d62-a76c-11f1-a1f6-8596f8c2fc95</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 08:18:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff8ec802-a76b-11f1-9b93-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T071929Z-2098391657-RC2JBNAFLHWL-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Susana Vera, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Churchillian moment? Macron in Britain amid scramble to boost European defence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence</link><description>
What can an 11th-century comic strip about the Norman Conquest of England tell us about the spectre of sea change in 2026 Europe? France’s president is on hand for the hottest ticket in London, the first-ever cross-Channel visit of the Bayeux Tapestry, which, for the record, is not a tapestry but a delicate scroll of embroidered cloth that chronicles a radical turning point in our continent’s history. Should France’s outgoing president and the British monarch who welcomes him be likened more to the defending Saxons or the invading Normans?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8350741c-a6f7-11f1-98e4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T173545Z-345916733-RC25BNAXXYSQ-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8350741c-a6f7-11f1-98e4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T173545Z-345916733-RC25BNAXXYSQ-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d32a966c-a6f6-11f1-9e00-cd657499c2a0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 07:39:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron, Burnham hold talks on migrants, EU after viewing Bayeux Tapestry in London</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron and UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham held their first talks on Thursday after meeting a day earlier at the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition at the British Museum. Topping the agenda were several issues, including migrant boats crossing the Channel, British-EU relations and the Ukraine war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a42059fa-a760-11f1-b937-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245663397453.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a42059fa-a760-11f1-b937-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245663397453.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63125fda-a760-11f1-9ea2-6bf5dcd88787</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 06:47:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a42059fa-a760-11f1-b937-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245663397453.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine warns Russian airspace ‘not safe’ in message to UN aviation watchdog</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine</link><description>
Ukraine urged the UN aviation agency to call for a full ban on flights through Russian airspace after President Volodymyr Zelensky warned it was becoming unsafe. Kyiv plans increased retaliation against intensified Russian strikes but would target only military facilities, Zelensky said, citing growing Ukrainian drone activity over Russia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3943762-9f52-11f1-839c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/d3bbc74c16e971757a0282ef4d645e2670b58f09.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3943762-9f52-11f1-839c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/d3bbc74c16e971757a0282ef4d645e2670b58f09.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22d4f998-a713-11f1-b7b0-d1850c402931</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 22:46:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3943762-9f52-11f1-839c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/d3bbc74c16e971757a0282ef4d645e2670b58f09.jpg">© Tetiana Dzhafarova, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Outrage in Malta as court acquits tycoon in investigative journalist murder case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder</link><description>
A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the 2017 car-bomb killing of investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia, a verdict that drew condemnation from her family and press freedom advocates. Her family said the acquittal denied Caruana Galizia justice, while her son called it a “terrible decision”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e575ea4-a714-11f1-96e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T211806Z-686920899-RC26BNAZQ7CO-RTRMADP-3-MALTA-DAPHNE-TRIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e575ea4-a714-11f1-96e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T211806Z-686920899-RC26BNAZQ7CO-RTRMADP-3-MALTA-DAPHNE-TRIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef7a451c-a717-11f1-a7ec-c1d6529d5029</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 21:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e575ea4-a714-11f1-96e8-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-02T211806Z-686920899-RC26BNAZQ7CO-RTRMADP-3-MALTA-DAPHNE-TRIAL.jpg">© Darrin Zammit Lupi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky warns airlines Russian skies not safe due to Ukraine drones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned Tuesday that his country's drones would make Russia's airspace "completely unsafe" for the duration of the war, drawing accusations of "state terrorism" from Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Former British Military Intelligence Officer Philip Ingram explains that Zelensky's warning is addressed to "those international airlines from the Middle East, from South East Asia, China included that are still operating into Moscow" adding that "it's all part of the information war and bringing the overall conflict to the Russian people".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28e9c598-7e7d-11f1-9486-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T130639Z-1873803642-RC2LZLA3LE8L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DRONES-GERMANY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28e9c598-7e7d-11f1-9486-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-12T130639Z-1873803642-RC2LZLA3LE8L-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-DRONES-GERMANY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9bc3e66c-a703-11f1-b090-33773faa09bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:32:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia blamed for explosive-laden drone found at German airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport</link><description>
After #Germany blamed #Russia for the explosive-laden #drone found at #Leipzig airport on August 4, #Berlin has introduced new sanctions against #Moscow. Namely, its consulate in #Bonn and the Russian House - a cultural centre thought to be a Russian #spy hub - in #Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6795890-a6e7-11f1-80d6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-Leipzig.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6795890-a6e7-11f1-80d6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-Leipzig.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8f38202-a6e7-11f1-837e-cd8816f6a8c6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 16:11:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany investigates suspected power substation sabotage, Russia summons German envoy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-germany-ivestigates-suspected-power-substation-sabotage-russia-summons-german-envoy</link><description>
Two incidents that disrupted power distribution systems in Germany are being investigated for sabotage, authorities said Wednesday, while one of them was also being examined for possible terrorism links. Meanwhile Russia said it was summoning Germany's charge d'affaires after Berlin blamed Moscow for last month's attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cbbf1e4-a6ca-11f1-a25f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6HY7WD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cbbf1e4-a6ca-11f1-a25f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6HY7WD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6af0d884-a6cb-11f1-94f1-511abfe4a3ce</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 13:15:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cbbf1e4-a6ca-11f1-a25f-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6HY7WD.jpg">© Tobias Schwarz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Drone incident in Germany has ‘hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism’, EU's Kallas says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-eu-summons-russia-envoys-eyes-sanctions-after-germany-drone-attack</link><description>
Last month's incident involving an explosive-laden drone at Leipzig airport bears "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism," EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said Wednesday. Germany has blamed Russia for the "hybrid attack". The EU has summoned the Russian envoy, and member states were doing the same, Kallas said. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16fcfed0-a6ce-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/813067157fdc4184191f8af106ecc712356737d7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16fcfed0-a6ce-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/813067157fdc4184191f8af106ecc712356737d7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1855e198-a6ce-11f1-9683-511abfe4a3ce</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 12:59:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16fcfed0-a6ce-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/813067157fdc4184191f8af106ecc712356737d7.jpg">© Paul Faith, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron urges France, UK to forge closer bond as Bayeux Tapestry goes on display in Britain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron called on France and Britain to forge closer ties on Wednesday as he joined King Charles III and Prime Minister Andy Burnham to mark the historic loan of the Bayeux Tapestry to the British Museum. Macron said the two allies could build a bond “as close as the threads” of the 950-year-old artwork, which depicts the Norman conquest of England.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da6989f8-a703-11f1-99e6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245663394956.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da6989f8-a703-11f1-99e6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245663394956.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">707c2f28-a66d-11f1-9426-1bc7a8b22ec1</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 01:27:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da6989f8-a703-11f1-99e6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245663394956.jpg">© Richard Pohle, AP via pool</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany blames Russia for airport drone incident, hits back with sanctions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-blames-russia-for-airport-drone-incident-hits-back-with-sanctions</link><description>
Germany on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted "hybrid attack" involving an explosive-laden drone at a strategic airport last month and announced diplomatic counter-measures. The European Union expressed "full solidarity" with Germany, NATO assured that it would defend its members and countries including Britain, Estonia and Poland offered strong backing. Germany will close Russia's consulate in the former capital Bonn later this month, and cancel the contract for the Russian House, a cultural centre in Berlin, said Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c8eefa4a-a646-11f1-a739-c9290005fc0e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 20:58:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Burnham pledges to restore hope as he makes his House of Commons debut as UK leader</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/burnham-pledges-to-restore-hope-as-he-makes-his-house-of-commons-debut-as-uk-leader</link><description>
Prime Minister Andy Burnham faced lawmakers in the House of Commons on Tuesday for the first time since becoming U.K. leader six weeks ago, with wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy, ease the cost of living and oversee a radical redistribution of power from London to Britain's regions. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Dr Martin Farr, Senior Lecturer in British Contemporary History at Newcastle University.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80a63c86-a618-11f1-b626-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1891369266a96ecf6cd7717-90115964.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80a63c86-a618-11f1-b626-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1891369266a96ecf6cd7717-90115964.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9905e0b4-a646-11f1-9875-7d1a514cfab9</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 20:54:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany blames Russia for Leipzig airport drone attack, orders Russian consulate closed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed</link><description>
Germany's government on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport on 4 August using an explosive-laden drone, and announced that it would shut down a Russian consulate among other measures against Moscow. French ​President Emmanuel Macron ​said he supported the ​adoption ‌of ⁠new European sanctions ‌against Russia after the attempted drone attack.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0569ab12-a626-11f1-8099-df4aff4c5350</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 17:00:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79b2ea30-a61a-11f1-b028-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-08T101129Z-1947811119-RC2CSMA5SMYP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-SECURITY-DRONES.jpg">© Axel Schmidt, Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What to know about the new UK PM's agenda as he faces lawmakers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers</link><description>
Since taking office on July 20, Burnham has traveled around the country promising to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of his predecessor Keir Starmer. Now, it's time for him to face lawmakers for the first time since he has taken office after an unusually long time without having to do so due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us what to know from his speech.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cc3533c-8438-11f1-98fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T120731Z-1505653970-RC2NHMAGF2Z5-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cc3533c-8438-11f1-98fd-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T120731Z-1505653970-RC2NHMAGF2Z5-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a6e7780-a619-11f1-8968-db76c1323643</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:39:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Replay: UK PM Andy Burnham faces lawmakers for first time since taking office</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office</link><description>
Rewatch UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's first speech to parliament since taking office six weeks prior.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80a63c86-a618-11f1-b626-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1891369266a96ecf6cd7717-90115964.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80a63c86-a618-11f1-b626-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1891369266a96ecf6cd7717-90115964.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">09332ec6-a617-11f1-8c3d-db76c1323643</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:22:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After 'unprecedented honeymoon', UK PM faces lawmakers for first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time</link><description>
Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on September 1 for the first time since becoming UK leader six weeks ago. This comes as the wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy and ease the cost of living. Andy Burnham has enjoyed quite a long time without facing lawmakers due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5dc73ba-84a7-11f1-a0fa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201430781165.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5dc73ba-84a7-11f1-a0fa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201430781165.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a49f9ae-a615-11f1-ada6-21b4b9529c13</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:10:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 12 killed and over a dozen injured in Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv</link><description>
Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured many more in Kyiv and the surrounding region early on September 1, authorities said, marking the sixth straight day of intense strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Those injured three children, just as Ukrainian pupils return to school. In a new tactic, Moscow has sent swarms of new jet-powered drones to ⁠plague Kyiv and nearby areas day and night, killing residents and damaging homes and warehouses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33f40dfc-a5f3-11f1-a5be-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T100315Z-704783314-RC2AANAPA26V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33f40dfc-a5f3-11f1-a5be-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-01T100315Z-704783314-RC2AANAPA26V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ee3246c-a612-11f1-851d-8d73d79a9abf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:56:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia's G20 US invitation severely criticised by European countries</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries</link><description>
Finance ministers and central bank governors from the group of 20 major economies are meeting for two days in Asheville, North Carolina. With the United States holding the rotating G20 presidency, Washington is trying to rally partners towards greater economic pressure on Iran and find ways to boost growth. But an unexpected attendee drew fierce criticism.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bf0ee0-a60b-11f1-9916-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T150853Z-251325442-RC2Q9NAYZ3N2-RTRMADP-3-G20-FINANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bf0ee0-a60b-11f1-9916-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T150853Z-251325442-RC2Q9NAYZ3N2-RTRMADP-3-G20-FINANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78719e2c-a602-11f1-968b-f9580e1f490b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:48:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine hopes for bolstered support as EU defence ministers meet in Dublin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hopes-for-bolstered-support-as-eu-defence-ministers-meet-in-dublin</link><description>
EU defence ministers grapple with bolstering Ukraine's air defences, as worries grow over Russia's campaign to destabilise Kyiv's European backers. This comes as Moscow is taking advantage of Kyiv running low on US-built air defence missiles to intensify its attacks on the country. EU ministers are also expected to discuss Russia's hybrid war against Ukraine's European allies. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ef9d6b8-a609-11f1-9d00-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203312063368.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ef9d6b8-a609-11f1-9d00-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203312063368.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">df9d4ff2-a601-11f1-9efa-f9580e1f490b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:34:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK needs 'substantial change', says PM Andy Burnham in maiden parliament speech</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office</link><description>
The United Kingdom's new Prime Minister Andy Burnham said the UK needed "substantial change" at his maiden speech in the House of Commons on Tuesday. Burnham has promised to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of predecessor Keir Starmer, who announced Tuesday that he would resign his seat in Parliament after 11 years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a20bd6ae-8432-11f1-9d23-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201431350183.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a20bd6ae-8432-11f1-9d23-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201431350183.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">880bab7a-a607-11f1-84bc-77a48fff9120</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:21:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a20bd6ae-8432-11f1-9d23-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201431350183.jpg">© Kirsty Wigglesworth, AP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Massive' Russian missile, drone attacks on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv</link><description>
Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured several more in Kyiv early on Tuesday, authorities said, in the sixth consecutive day of strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Russia, which began its full-scale invasion of its smaller neighbour in 2022, has escalated its air attacks in recent months, as gains made on the ground have slowed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/274ebab2-a5f2-11f1-9fb1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/miniukraine.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/274ebab2-a5f2-11f1-9fb1-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/miniukraine.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41e0ad72-a5f2-11f1-8c64-039419ac9708</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 10:50:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia fired over 2,800 drones at Ukraine in August amid war tactic change</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change</link><description>
Over the course of the month of August, Russia launched more than 2,800 jet-propelled drones at Ukraine, a type of drone that is harder to shoot down. That has come with a massive uptick in the number of drones used, considerind those now found on the frontline are quite a new model: Ukrainian authorities say they are pressed into service almost immediately after leaving the factory. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry looks at those new drones, and how Russia is using them to try and change the course of the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66b0ba4c-a5e9-11f1-801f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T074311Z-523755993-RC2I7NA0XC1F-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-ZAPORIZHZHIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66b0ba4c-a5e9-11f1-801f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T074311Z-523755993-RC2I7NA0XC1F-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-ZAPORIZHZHIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93c8c1ca-a5e2-11f1-970e-4312efd22778</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:49:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia targets Kyiv and its region for sixth consecutive night of attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks</link><description>
At least nine people have been killed and 14 injured in Russian strikes on Ukraine overnight. Moscow targeted Kyiv and the wider region in the attack, hitting a railway depot in the Kyiv. Russia's defence ministry said it had also struck infrastructure in the Southern Odesa region. Russia has intensified strikes on the beleaguered Ukrainian cities in recent weeks disrupting the daily lives of millions of people and triggering up to a dozen air-raid alerts a day.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e95510d8-a5d0-11f1-9a29-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YJ6T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e95510d8-a5d0-11f1-9a29-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YJ6T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66625fc6-a5e1-11f1-8e7e-4312efd22778</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:39:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Lake Annecy gun linked to unsolved 2012 murder of British family in French Alps</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline</link><description>
French officials say a Luger pistol fished out from the bottom of Lake Annecy shows similarities to the weapon used in the notorious 2012 killings of a British-Iraqi family and a French cyclist in the nearby village of Chevaline, opening up a new lead in a case that has befuddled investigators for over a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/478d5106-7494-11ec-a6b7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/chavaline%201301.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/478d5106-7494-11ec-a6b7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/chavaline%201301.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2260e544-a5d8-11f1-91e4-599faa1a754c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 08:21:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/478d5106-7494-11ec-a6b7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/chavaline%201301.jpg">© Philippe Desmazes, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Safe days in Russian skies are over,' warns Zelensky</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Tuesday warned airlines, insurance firms and passengers that Russian airspace would be "completely unsafe" and filled with Ukrainian drones for the duration of the war. His address came after a night of relentless Russian bombardment in Ukraine, which killed at least a dozen people. Read our liveblog to see how all the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/266a8d7c-a5f4-11f1-ad51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YZ4NW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/266a8d7c-a5f4-11f1-ad51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YZ4NW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">636397d2-a5c7-11f1-856a-b31f71a56ada</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 06:04:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/266a8d7c-a5f4-11f1-ad51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6YZ4NW.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv kills at least eight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four</link><description>
A massive Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv and its surrounding region killed at least eight people and wounded more than a dozen overnight, Ukrainian officials said Tuesday, as children prepared to return to school amid heightened fears of further strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3254e58-a5ab-11f1-a88b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242478432296.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3254e58-a5ab-11f1-a88b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242478432296.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99553aa0-a5ac-11f1-ac37-232b90c8c885</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 02:26:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3254e58-a5ab-11f1-a88b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242478432296.jpg">© Francisco Seco, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
